  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If \\(x\\) is real and \\(4y^2+4xy+x+6=0,\\) then the complete set of values of \\(x\\) for which \\(y\\) is real, is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(x\\leq-2\\) or \\(x\\geq3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(x\\leq2\\) or \\(x\\geq3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(x\\leq-3\\) or \\(x\\geq2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(-3\\leq x\\leq2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(-2\\leq x\\leq3\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1966-p23.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "As a quadratic in \\(y,\\) the equation has discriminant \\[ \\begin{aligned} &(4x)^2-16(x+6)\\\\ &\\qquad=16(x-3)(x+2). \\end{aligned} \\] This is nonnegative exactly when \\(x\\leq-2\\) or \\(x\\geq3.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Treat the equation as a quadratic in \\(y\\)",
        "Require its discriminant \\(16(x-3)(x+2)\\) to be nonnegative"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
